From f07d5f2307ea7e01c7d8375ade82247044448bea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calogero Mandracchia <calogero@efebia.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:50:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] tui: show status line items from an external JSON file

When tui.status_line_file or CODEX_STATUS_LINE_FILE names a file, its
fields can be placed in tui.status_line as file:<key> items, next to the
built-in ones. Any program can write the file as
{"fields": {"<key>": "<text>"}}.

A background thread polls the file's metadata and re-reads it only when
it changes, so rendering never touches the file system. Missing files,
invalid JSON and unusable values hide the items without warnings; long
values are truncated. {session_id} in the path expands to the session
shown by the TUI, and values of the previous file are dropped when the
session changes.

The /statusline picker lists the configured file items and the fields
present in the file, and saving keeps file: items instead of dropping
them as unknown ids.
